decoder.js and decoder.wasm are prebuilt releases of the FFmpeg-based decoder

  https://github.com/chandler-stimson/decoder.js/releases/tag/0.1.2

src/ holds the buildable source this extension is migrating to. It is derived
from the upstream project with the following changes:

  * batch output is buffered (the original issued one fwrite per 4-byte
    sample, which dominated the decode time of large files)
  * an incremental streaming API (decoder_open / decoder_pull /
    decoder_seek / decoder_close) fed through JS callbacks so that playback
    can start before the whole file is downloaded and decoded
  * a use-after-free in the batch clean-up path was fixed

Build (requires emsdk, git, make, pkg-config):

  cd src && bash build.sh

The output (decoder.js, decoder.wasm) is produced in this directory and must
replace the checked-in binaries above. The batch entry point `decoder` keeps
its 0.1.2 contract, so the binaries can be swapped without any extension
changes; the streaming API is consumed by worker.js afterwards.

A GitHub workflow (.github/workflows/build-decoder.yml) builds the artifacts
automatically on changes to this folder.
